Z||000010||Oreif||12-14-2001||10:56 PM||||IRM is a family owned business. Although they have been slow to respond, They are not too bad to deal with once you get to talk with them. The Fiero Store catalogs are more "professional" looking because they usually have money left over from the Research and Development Department. Instead of spending lots of $$$$ on a staff of engineers and designers, They just buy Rodney's stuff and copy it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Formula88||12-15-2001||12:36 AM||||Well, the 4 month delay is ridiculous, but I've gotten photocopied and stapled catalogs from Rodney Dickman, too.  No one here debates the top notch quality of his work.  He just chose not to spend the extra money on publishing a glossy color catalog.  <P>With the Fiero Stores prices, they can afford to splurge.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Doni Hagan||12-15-2001||02:35 AM||||Don't hold the delay getting a catalogue out to you against IRM. I've dealt with them on a couple of occasions and would again...I'll admit that the only thing that's changed in their catalogue for years are the prices themselves and the notice of discontinued items (rocker panels/Indy scoop/etc..) But other than the dorky hat pics in the back, their stuff is still good. <P>Ask for Barbara...nice folks to do business with.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/WAY2SLO_16.jpg"> ||||reg||1
